--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-22-fix-json-patch-conformance/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` iterates with `forEach`, which skips holes of sparse arrays, and calls `parsePointer` directly, so pointer syntax errors escape as `JsonPointerError`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Iterate with an index loop so every position is visited; a hole is not an object and is rejected.
+- Wrap `parsePointer` in `pointerOf` and rethrow `JsonPointerError` as `JsonPatchError` with the operation index.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- Other behaviour (atomic failure by working on a clone, remove of root throwing, move/copy/test semantics) was reviewed against RFC 6902 and is already conformant.
