@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Users of `applyPatch` report results that differ from RFC 6902. A review of patch checking and application found a malformed patch that is accepted and failures that surface inconsistently.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- A patch array with holes (sparse array) is rejected instead of silently skipping the holes.
+- Invalid JSON Pointers in `path` or `from` are reported as `JsonPatchError`, like every other patch failure, rather than leaking `JsonPointerError`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: validation of the patch and the error type of failures.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/patch.ts` and `test/patch.test.ts`. No new dependencies; `json-pointer` is unchanged.
